Original change's description:
> [maglev] Prewalk skipped bytecodes on polymorphic continuation abort
>
> When a polymorphic property-load continuation aborts partway through
> (e.g. inside `receiver.f(class extends (gate(), holder.q) {})` after
> entering the class scope),
> AdvanceThroughContinuationForPolymorphicPropertyLoad previously advanced
> the bytecode iterator to the end of the continuation without calling
> PrewalkBytecode(). Any skipped PopContext bytecodes were missed, leaving
> the nested scope active and causing dead-code scanning of a subsequent
> SuspendGenerator to record stale ScopeInfo on the generator resume
> target.
>
> Call PrewalkBytecode() while advancing through the remaining
> continuation bytecodes so scope tracking stays balanced on abort.
>
